    "properAnswer": "Autoboxing is the automatic conversion that the Java compiler makes between primitive types and their corresponding wrapper classes (e.g., `int` to `Integer`). Introduced in Java 5, when you write `Integer num = 10;`, `javac` automatically converts it to `Integer num = Integer.valueOf(10);` in bytecode. The reverse process is unboxing, which converts an `Integer` object back to an `int` primitive via `.intValue()`."
