    "properAnswer": "A Java `switch` statement evaluates a primitive, Enum, or String selector expression and jumps directly to the matching `case` block. At the bytecode level, the JVM compiles switch statements into either:\n1) **`tableswitch`**: Used when case values are contiguous (O(1) index jump table lookups).\n2) **`lookupswitch`**: Used when case values are sparse (O(log N) binary search lookup).\nIf no `break`, `yield`, or `return` statement is encountered inside a matched `case`, execution continues down into subsequent cases regardless of their condition values (**Fall-Through**)."
