    "properAnswer": "Syntactically, the `default` case can be placed **anywhere** inside a classic `switch` block (top, middle, or bottom). If no `case` label matches, the JVM will jump to `default` regardless of its physical position in the block. However, if `default` is placed at the top or middle **without a `break` statement**, execution will fall through into subsequent `case` blocks! Therefore, convention and enterprise coding guidelines mandate placing `default` as the **very last case**, acting as a clean fallback."
