    "properAnswer": "Introduced in Java 7, **try-with-resources** is an Automatic Resource Management (ARM) mechanism that automatically closes resources when exiting the `try` block scope, regardless of whether execution completes normally or throws an exception.\n\n**Key Requirements & Evolution**:\n1) **`AutoCloseable` Contract**: Any resource declared inside `try (Resource res = new Resource())` MUST implement `java.lang.AutoCloseable` (or `java.io.Closeable`).\n2) **Java 9+ Improvement**: You no longer need to declare a new local variable inside the header; existing `effectively final` variables can be passed directly: `try (existingReader) { ... }`."
