    "properAnswer": "You iterate over an array using the enhanced `for` loop (for-each) with the syntax `for (ElementType element : array)`:\n\n```java\nint[] numbers = {10, 20, 30};\nfor (int num : numbers) {\n    System.out.println(num);\n}\n```\n**Behind the Scenes**:\nFor arrays, `javac` **desugars** the enhanced `for` loop into a standard indexed loop (`for (int i = 0; i < numbers.length; i++) int num = numbers[i];`).\n**Limitations**:\n- **No Index Tracking**: You don't have access to the current index `i`.\n- **No Array Reassignment**: Reassigning `num = 50;` inside the loop only changes the local copy `num`, leaving `numbers[i]` untouched."
