    "properAnswer": "In Java, the **`assert`** statement (introduced in JDK 1.4) is a debugging tool used by developers to test internal assumptions (invariants) in code.\n\n**Syntax**:\n- `assert condition;`\n- `assert condition : \"ErrorMessage\";`\n\n**Key Characteristics**:\n1) **Disabled by Default**: Assertions do NOT run in production by default. They must be explicitly enabled using the JVM flag `-ea` (`java -ea MainClass`).\n2) **Failure Behavior**: If the condition evaluates to `false`, the JVM throws an `AssertionError`."
