    "properAnswer": "A **Static Initializer** (or static block) is a `static { ... }` block inside a class used to perform complex initialization of `static` fields.\n\n**Under the Hood & Mechanics**:\n1) **Bytecode `<clinit>`**: The compiler merges all inline static variable initializations and static blocks in text order into a single bytecode method named `<clinit>()`.\n2) **Thread Safety**: The JVM automatically acquires a class initialization lock, guaranteeing that static initializers execute in a completely thread-safe manner exactly **once** per ClassLoader.\n3) **Failure Mode**: Throwing an unhandled exception inside a static block results in a fatal `java.lang.ExceptionInInitializerError`."
