    "properAnswer": "Here are standard practical examples demonstrating tokenizing techniques in Java:\n\n**1. Simple Array Extraction (`String.split`)**:\n```java\nString csv = \"apple,banana,orange\";\nString[] fruits = csv.split(\",\");\n// Result: [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"orange\"]\n```\n\n**2. High-Performance Tokenizing (`Pattern.compile`)**:\n```java\n// Pre-compiled pattern avoids re-parsing regex inside high-throughput loops\nprivate static final Pattern CSV_PATTERN = Pattern.compile(\"\\\\s*,\\\\s*\");\nString[] tokens = CSV_PATTERN.split(\"apple , banana , orange\");\n```\n\n**3. Stream Parsing with Primitives (`java.util.Scanner`)**:\n```java\nString data = \"100, 200, 300\";\nScanner scanner = new Scanner(data).useDelimiter(\"\\\\s*,\\\\s*\");\nwhile (scanner.hasNextInt()) {\n    int value = scanner.nextInt(); // Directly parses primitive ints\n}\n```"
