    "properAnswer": "Deserialization reconstructs live objects from a byte stream using **`ObjectInputStream`**:\n\n```java\ntry (FileInputStream fileIn = new FileInputStream(\"user.ser\");\n     ObjectInputStream in = new ObjectInputStream(fileIn)) {\n    \n    User user = (User) in.readObject(); // Reconstructs object on heap\n    System.out.println(\"Deserialized User: \" + user.getUsername());\n}\n```\n\n**Crucial Execution Details**:\n1) **No Constructor Execution**: The serialized class's constructor is **skipped**. The JVM uses `ReflectionFactory` to instantiate the object and inject field values directly.\n2) **`serialVersionUID` Validation**: If the `serialVersionUID` in the stream does not match the loaded class's `serialVersionUID`, `InvalidClassException` is thrown.\n3) **Security Modernization**: Always use Java 9+ `ObjectInputFilter` to validate classes before deserialization to protect against Remote Code Execution (RCE) attacks."
