    "properAnswer": "The **`Set`** interface extends `Collection` to model mathematical sets, enforcing strict element uniqueness:\n\n**Core Contracts**:\n1) **No Duplicates**: A `Set` cannot contain duplicate elements ($e1.equals(e2)$). Calling `add(e)` with an existing element returns `false` and leaves the set unchanged.\n2) **No Index Operations**: Unlike `List`, `Set` does not provide index-based access (`get(int)`) because elements have no inherent numeric index.\n3) **Null Handling**: Permits at most one `null` element (except `TreeSet` which rejects `null` entirely)."
