      "Space vs Time Trade-off: Higher load factor (> 0.75) saves memory but increases hash bucket collision frequency; lower load factor (< 0.75) reduces collisions but wastes array memory.",
      "Default 0.75 Trade-off Rationale: 0.75 provides an optimal mathematical balance between search time and space utilization under Poisson element distributions."
