    "properAnswer": "**Load factor** is a float metric that determines when a hash-based collection (`HashMap`, `HashSet`) resizes its array capacity:\n\n**Threshold Calculation**:\n$$\\text{Threshold} = \\text{Capacity} \\times \\text{Load Factor}$$\n- With default capacity **16** and default load factor **0.75**, the map doubles its capacity to **32** once **12** entries are inserted.\n\n**Trade-off**:\n- **Higher Load Factor**: Reduces memory usage but increases hash collisions, slowing down `get()` and `put()`.\n- **Lower Load Factor**: Minimizes collisions but consumes more memory and triggers frequent rehashing."
