    "properAnswer": "To restrict generics to a specific class or its superclasses, use a **Lower Bounded Wildcard** (`super` keyword):\n\n```java\npublic static void addNumbers(List<? super Integer> list) {\n    list.add(10); // Safe to insert Integer or its subclasses\n    list.add(20);\n}\n```\n- **Allowed Arguments**: `List<Integer>`, `List<Number>`, or `List<Object>`.\n- **PECS Principle**: **Producer Extends, Consumer Super**. Use `? super T` when your collection **consumes** (writes) data."
