    "properAnswer": "To create a thread by extending `Thread`:\n\n```java\nclass WorkerThread extends Thread {\n    @Override\n    public void run() {\n        System.out.println(\"Running in thread: \" + Thread.currentThread().getName());\n    }\n}\n\n// Instantiation & Execution:\nWorkerThread t = new WorkerThread();\nt.start(); // Creates native OS thread and invokes run()\n```\n- **Important Rule**: Always call **`start()`**, not `run()`. Calling `run()` executes code synchronously in the main caller thread."
