    "properAnswer": "The **`wait()`** method pauses thread execution while releasing the acquired monitor lock:\n\n```java\nsynchronized (lock) {\n    while (!condition) { // While loop prevents spurious wakeups\n        lock.wait(); // Releases monitor lock & pauses thread\n    }\n    // Execute logic after condition becomes true\n}\n```\n- **Key Difference**: `Thread.sleep()` **retains** locks, whereas `Object.wait()` **releases** the lock so other threads can proceed."
