    "properAnswer": "Java Stream pipelines consist of two types of operations:\n\n1) **Intermediate Operations** (Lazy): Transform a stream into another stream (`filter()`, `map()`, `flatMap()`). They **do not execute** until a terminal operation is called.\n2) **Terminal Operations** (Eager): Trigger execution of the stream pipeline and produce a result or side-effect (`collect()`, `reduce()`, `forEach()`). Once invoked, the stream is consumed."
