    "properAnswer": "Comparison between **`supplyAsync()`** and **`runAsync()`**:\n\n1) **`CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(Supplier<T>)`**: Executes asynchronously and **returns a result** `T`. Used for data retrieval or computation.\n2) **`CompletableFuture.runAsync(Runnable)`**: Executes asynchronously for **side-effects only** and returns `CompletableFuture<Void>`.\n3) **Best Practice**: Always supply a dedicated **`Executor`** pool parameter (`supplyAsync(supplier, customExecutor)`) to avoid consuming threads from the shared default `ForkJoinPool.commonPool()`."
