    "properAnswer": "**Structured Concurrency in Java 21 (`StructuredTaskScope`)**:\n\n```java\npublic Response fetchUserData(String userId) throws Exception {\n    try (var scope = new StructuredTaskScope.ShutdownOnFailure()) {\n        // Fork subtasks on Virtual Threads concurrently\n        Supplier<User> userTask = scope.fork(() -> userService.getUser(userId));\n        Supplier<Order> orderTask = scope.fork(() -> orderService.getOrders(userId));\n\n        scope.join();           // Wait for both subtasks\n        scope.throwIfFailed(); // Propagate exception if ANY subtask failed\n\n        // Both succeeded - combine results cleanly\n        return new Response(userTask.get(), orderTask.get());\n    } // Auto-closes scope and cancels any lingering subtasks on exit\n}\n```"
