    "properAnswer": "**Decorator Pattern Implementation**:\n\n```java\n// Shared Interface\npublic interface Coffee {\n    double getCost();\n    String getDescription();\n}\n\n// Base Component\npublic class SimpleCoffee implements Coffee {\n    public double getCost() { return 2.0; }\n    public String getDescription() { return \"Simple Coffee\"; }\n}\n\n// Abstract Decorator\npublic abstract class CoffeeDecorator implements Coffee {\n    protected final Coffee decoratedCoffee;\n    public CoffeeDecorator(Coffee coffee) { this.decoratedCoffee = coffee; }\n    public double getCost() { return decoratedCoffee.getCost(); }\n    public String getDescription() { return decoratedCoffee.getDescription(); }\n}\n\n// Concrete Decorator\npublic class MilkDecorator extends CoffeeDecorator {\n    public MilkDecorator(Coffee coffee) { super(coffee); }\n    @Override public double getCost() { return super.getCost() + 0.5; }\n    @Override public String getDescription() { return super.getDescription() + \", Milk\"; }\n}\n// Usage: Coffee myCoffee = new MilkDecorator(new SimpleCoffee()); // Cost: 2.5\n```"
