    "properAnswer": "**JDK Dynamic Proxy Implementation**:\n\n```java\npublic interface UserService {\n    void createUser(String username);\n}\n\npublic class UserServiceImpl implements UserService {\n    public void createUser(String username) {\n        System.out.println(\"User created: \" + username);\n    }\n}\n\n// Dynamic Proxy Handler adding transaction logging\npublic class LoggingInvocationHandler implements InvocationHandler {\n    private final Object target;\n    public LoggingInvocationHandler(Object target) { this.target = target; }\n\n    @Override\n    public Object invoke(Object proxy, Method method, Object[] args) throws Throwable {\n        System.out.println(\"[BEFORE] Starting transaction for: \" + method.getName());\n        Object result = method.invoke(target, args);\n        System.out.println(\"[AFTER] Transaction committed.\");\n        return result;\n    }\n}\n// Instantiation: UserService proxy = (UserService) Proxy.newProxyInstance(\n//    UserService.class.getClassLoader(), new Class<?>[]{UserService.class}, new LoggingInvocationHandler(new UserServiceImpl()));\n```"
