    "properAnswer": "**Chain of Responsibility Implementation**:\n\n```java\npublic abstract class RequestHandler {\n    protected RequestHandler next;\n    public RequestHandler setNext(RequestHandler next) { this.next = next; return next; }\n    public abstract void handle(String request);\n}\n\npublic class AuthHandler extends RequestHandler {\n    public void handle(String request) {\n        if (!request.contains(\"token\")) throw new SecurityException(\"Unauthorized\");\n        if (next != null) next.handle(request); // Pass along chain\n    }\n}\n\npublic class RateLimitHandler extends RequestHandler {\n    public void handle(String request) {\n        System.out.println(\"Rate limit passed.\");\n        if (next != null) next.handle(request);\n    }\n}\n// Chain Assembly: AuthHandler auth = new AuthHandler(); auth.setNext(new RateLimitHandler()); auth.handle(req);\n```"
