    "properAnswer": "**Thread-Safe Token Bucket Rate Limiter**:\n\n```java\npublic class TokenBucketRateLimiter {\n    private final long capacity;\n    private final double refillRatePerNano;\n    private double tokens;\n    private long lastRefillNano;\n\n    public TokenBucketRateLimiter(long capacity, long tokensPerSecond) {\n        this.capacity = capacity;\n        this.refillRatePerNano = tokensPerSecond / 1_000_000_000.0;\n        this.tokens = capacity;\n        this.lastRefillNano = System.nanoTime();\n    }\n\n    public synchronized boolean tryConsume() {\n        long now = System.nanoTime();\n        // Lazy refill tokens based on elapsed nanoseconds\n        double generatedTokens = (now - lastRefillNano) * refillRatePerNano;\n        tokens = Math.min(capacity, tokens + generatedTokens);\n        lastRefillNano = now;\n\n        if (tokens >= 1.0) {\n            tokens -= 1.0;\n            return true; // Request allowed\n        }\n        return false; // Rate limit exceeded (HTTP 429)\n    }\n}\n```"
