    "properAnswer": "**Thread-Safe TTL Cache Implementation**:\n\n```java\npublic class SimpleTtlCache<K, V> {\n    private record CacheEntry<V>(V value, long expireAt) {\n        boolean isExpired() { return System.currentTimeMillis() > expireAt; }\n    }\n\n    private final Map<K, CacheEntry<V>> map = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();\n    private final ScheduledExecutorService cleaner = Executors.newSingleThreadScheduledExecutor();\n\n    public SimpleTtlCache(long cleanupPeriodSec) {\n        // Active Eviction: Periodic background cleanup sweep\n        cleaner.scheduleAtFixedRate(this::evictExpired, cleanupPeriodSec, cleanupPeriodSec, TimeUnit.SECONDS);\n    }\n\n    public void put(K key, V value, long ttlMs) {\n        map.put(key, new CacheEntry<>(value, System.currentTimeMillis() + ttlMs));\n    }\n\n    public V get(K key) {\n        CacheEntry<V> entry = map.get(key);\n        if (entry == null) return null;\n        if (entry.isExpired()) { // Passive Eviction\n            map.remove(key);\n            return null;\n        }\n        return entry.value();\n    }\n\n    private void evictExpired() {\n        map.entrySet().removeIf(e -> e.getValue().isExpired());\n    }\n}\n```"
