    "properAnswer": "**Kahn's BFS Topological Sort Algorithm ($O(V + E)$ Time)**:\n\n```java\npublic class TopologicalSort {\n    public int[] findOrder(int numCourses, int[][] prerequisites) {\n        List<List<Integer>> adj = new ArrayList<>();\n        int[] inDegree = new int[numCourses];\n        for (int i = 0; i < numCourses; i++) adj.add(new ArrayList<>());\n\n        for (int[] pre : prerequisites) {\n            adj.get(pre[1]).add(pre[0]); // Edge pre[1] -> pre[0]\n            inDegree[pre[0]]++;\n        }\n\n        Queue<Integer> queue = new LinkedList<>();\n        for (int i = 0; i < numCourses; i++) {\n            if (inDegree[i] == 0) queue.offer(i); // Start with 0 in-degree nodes\n        }\n\n        int[] order = new int[numCourses];\n        int idx = 0;\n        while (!queue.isEmpty()) {\n            int curr = queue.poll();\n            order[idx++] = curr;\n            for (int neighbor : adj.get(curr)) {\n                inDegree[neighbor]--;\n                if (inDegree[neighbor] == 0) queue.offer(neighbor);\n            }\n        }\n        return (idx == numCourses) ? order : new int[0]; // Empty array if cycle detected\n    }\n}\n```"
