    "properAnswer": "**Cycle Detection in Directed Graph (DFS Recursion Stack)**:\n\n```java\npublic class DirectedCycle {\n    public boolean isCyclic(int V, List<List<Integer>> adj) {\n        boolean[] visited = new boolean[V];\n        boolean[] inStack = new boolean[V];\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < V; i++) {\n            if (!visited[i]) {\n                if (dfs(i, visited, inStack, adj)) return true;\n            }\n        }\n        return false;\n    }\n\n    private boolean dfs(int node, boolean[] visited, boolean[] inStack, List<List<Integer>> adj) {\n        visited[node] = true;\n        inStack[node] = true; // Mark node in current active stack\n\n        for (int neighbor : adj.get(node)) {\n            if (!visited[neighbor]) {\n                if (dfs(neighbor, visited, inStack, adj)) return true;\n            } else if (inStack[neighbor]) {\n                return true; // Encircled back to active recursion stack -> Cycle!\n            }\n        }\n        inStack[node] = false; // Backtrack: Remove node from stack\n        return false;\n    }\n}\n```"
